In Summary!
=LET(
data,
VSTACK(
FILTER(Breakfast!B:C, Breakfast!A:A=TRUE),
FILTER(Lunch!B:C, Lunch!A:A=TRUE),
FILTER(Dinner!B:C, Dinner!A:A=TRUE)
),
data
)

------

=LET(
    GetItems, LAMBDA(sheet_range, flag_range, label,
        IFERROR(
            HSTACK(EXPAND(label, ROWS(FILTER(sheet_range, flag_range=TRUE)), , label), FILTER(sheet_range, flag_range=TRUE)),
            {"",""}
        )
    ),
    Combined, VSTACK(
        GetItems(Breakfast!B2:C100, Breakfast!A2:A100, "Breakfast"),
        GetItems(Lunch!B2:C100, Lunch!A2:A100, "Lunch"),
        GetItems(Dinner!B2:C100, Dinner!A2:A100, "Dinner")
    ),
    FILTER(Combined, CHOOSECOLS(Combined, 2) <> "")
)

Why this version is better:
Error Handling: By using IFERROR, the formula won't crash if you haven't picked a breakfast yet.

Context: It uses HSTACK and EXPAND to automatically add the word "Breakfast", "Lunch", or "Dinner" next to the items.

Dynamic Range: It assumes your data goes down to row 100, but it filters out the empty rows at the end so your summary stays tight.

Quick Setup Tip
When using VSTACK with FILTER, ensure your columns (B and C) match across all sheets. If "Breakfast" has 2 columns of data but "Lunch" only has 1, VSTACK will return an error.
